## How to attach a real adapter

Every mock adapter file contains a marked block:

```ts
// ─── REAL ADAPTER ATTACHMENT POINT ─────────────────────────────
// Replace createMockAdapter's internal MockTransport with ...
```

To connect a real system, replace the body of that file's `createMockAdapter(...)` call with a class/object implementing `AgentSystemAdapter` (or `ObsidianAdapter` for the Brain), then register it in `src/lib/connectors/registry.ts`. Nothing in `app/` or `components/` needs to change — they only ever call the adapter interface.

Per-system attachment targets (also listed as disabled fields on each row in `/registry`):

| Connector | File | Real transport |
|---|---|---|
| Claude / FCC | `mock/claude-fcc.ts` | CLI bridge (spawn `claude`, stream stdout) or Claude API |
| Hermes | `mock/hermes.ts` | Hermes REST API or CLI/gateway |
| OpenClaw | `mock/openclaw.ts` | OpenClaw CLI, gateway, or API |
| Paperclip | `mock/paperclip.ts` | Paperclip API, CLI, or direct database adapter |
| n8n | `mock/n8n.ts` | n8n REST API (workflows/executions) or inbound webhooks |
| AGY | `mock/agy.ts` | AGY orchestrator API |
| Obsidian (Shared Brain) | `mock/obsidian-instance.ts` | Local filesystem vault, Obsidian Local REST API plugin, Obsidian MCP server, or CLI/file-watcher fallback |
| Browser Agents | `mock/browser-agents.ts` | CDP/Playwright or a claude-in-chrome-style bridge |

Adding a **new** agent system requires zero UI changes: write one adapter module (`createMockAdapter({...})` to start, or a real transport directly) plus its seed data, then add one line to `registry.ts`.

